# SmartClo settings
# run.bat makes a copy of this file called settings.env the first time. Edit settings.env
# (not this example), save it, then ask for a new reset code. No restart needed.
# Never share settings.env or upload it to GitHub: it holds your email password.
# No quotes needed around values.

# ---------------- Password reset emails (Gmail) ----------------
# 1. Google Account > Security > turn ON 2-Step Verification
# 2. Open https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords and create an App Password
# 3. Paste the 16 letters below (spaces are fine)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
SMTP_FROM=

# Port 587 = STARTTLS (normal for Gmail), port 465 = SSL. Use one or the other.
# SMTP_FROM: leave empty to use SMTP_USER (Gmail only sends as your own address).

# ---------------- Security (optional) ----------------
# SECRET_KEY signs the login cookies. If you leave it out, a random one is created once and
# saved in secret_key.txt. Only set it here if you want to choose your own long random value.
# SECRET_KEY=
